# std.ownership: the traits that give a type ownership semantics
# (spec/lang/13-ownership.md#ownership-traits). Both are prelude names
# (spec/lang/10-modules.md#prelude); the compiler knows them by name.

## A marker for a type whose every value is borrowed: each use writes
## `^T` or `^mut T`, never a plain `T`.
## See [own.own-only.marker](../../spec/lang/13-ownership.md#r-own.own-only.marker).
pub trait OwnOnly

## A destructor: `drop` runs when a value of the type is dropped.
## Only an `OwnOnly` type implements it.
## See [own.drop-own.trait](../../spec/lang/13-ownership.md#r-own.drop-own.trait).
pub trait DropOwn < OwnOnly:
    fn drop(^mut self) -> void

@intrinsic("drop")
## Ends `value` now: drops it, which runs its type's `drop` when the value
## owns; the compiler supplies the body at each type.
## See [Drops](../../spec/lang/13-ownership.md#drops).
pub fn drop[T](value: T) -> void:
    panic("intrinsic")
